<title>UK: Bangladesh buys cargo white sugar at $347.95 -trad.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh buys cargo white sugar at $347.95 -trad.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh bought 12,500 tonnes of 150 ICUMSA white sugar at $347.95 per tonne c &amp; f basis, sugar traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Monday market sources said Bangladesh had paid a leading London trader house around $346 per tonne for the low-quality cargo.</p>
<p>The shipment period specified in last week's tender was March 11/April 11, they said, adding that the sugar was likely to be Indian in origin.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
